course: dictionary
lesson: 11167
title: Reading the wind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A windsock is a word you may meet at an airport, on a field or on a boat. You may not know it yet, but the sentence around it gives you clues. «A windsock shows which way the wind blows, and pilots take off into the wind.» Something that shows the wind must be a useful sort of thing to have.
explain: A windsock is a cloth tube on a pole. When the wind blows into it, it fills up and points the way the wind is going. Try your meaning in the sentence: «A cloth tube shows which way the wind blows» still makes sense, so you have worked it out.
explain: The sentence also tells you why it matters. Pilots take off into the wind because «it gives the wings more air flowing over them». Air moving over the wings helps the plane lift off, so the windsock helps the pilot choose the right way to face.
fact: A windsock is a cloth tube on a pole.
fact: A windsock fills with wind and shows which way the wind is blowing.
fact: A windsock also shows how strongly the wind is blowing: a strong wind fills it out more.
fact: «A windsock shows which way the wind blows, and pilots take off into the wind.»
fact: Windsocks are used at airports, airfields and on boats, and in weather and science lessons about measuring wind.
exercise: «A windsock shows which way the wind blows, and pilots take off into the wind.» What does a windsock show? | What time it is | How tall the pole is | *Which way the wind is blowing | The name of the airport
exercise: What is a windsock? | A metal bird that sings in the breeze | A type of boat sail that moves the boat forward | A small wind-up toy | *A cloth tube on a pole that fills with wind
exercise: Why do pilots take off into the wind? | Because the runway is shorter that way | Because the wind makes the plane heavier | *Because it gives the wings more air flowing over them | Because the wind is always quieter there
test: At an airport, the windsock hangs straight out from its pole. What does this tell you? | The windsock is broken and useless | *The wind is blowing strongly | The wind has stopped completely | The pole has fallen over
test: What can a windsock help a sailor or a weather scientist do? | *See which way and how hard the wind is blowing | Cook a warm meal | Count the clouds in the sky | Measure how deep the sea is
exam: Which sentence best explains what a windsock is? | It is a sock for keeping feet warm on a cold day | *It shows which way and how strongly the wind is blowing | It makes the wind blow faster across the field | It is a sail that pushes the boat forward
